DTSTAMP:20260704T034947Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260703T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260703T223000
SUMMARY:Music & Fireworks in Windsor
DESCRIPTION:Sonoma-Marin Brat Pack\nKaboom Windsor is a great place to sta
 rt your holiday weekend! Bring a blanket and lawn chair\, food\, cooler *o
 r purchase food & drink on-site. Tickets are $10 (cash & card accepted wit
 h express lane for cash) and proceeds go to help fund local kids programs.
  Once you're in the gate\, you're in\, so plan accordingly.\n\nMusic lineu
 p is as follows:\n\n4pm - gates open\n4-5.30 DJ Rolando\n6-7 Dry Creek Sta
 tion\n7.45-9.30 Joose\n9.30 National Anthem\n9.45 - fireworks\n\nSMART run
 ning late night and bicycle parking just outide park. Make your celebratio
 n easy and stress-free\, SMART will offer two special southbound return tr
 ains on July 3 departing Windsor at 10:20 pm and 10:50 p.m. The return tra
 in will run as far as the Petaluma Downtown Station\, providing a safe and
  convenient ride home after the show.\n\n*OK TO BRING:\nFood | Blankets | 
 Chairs | Soda | Water | Cameras | Coolers (no larger than 60qts) *Coolers 
 and bags inspected at gate\n\nPROHIBITED:\nGlass Bottles | Outside Alcohol
  | BBQs | Pop-Up Tents | Weapons | Fireworks | Animals | Drones | Umbrella
 s\n\nPARKING AND ROAD CLOSURES:\nAttendees who utilize the Windsor High Sc
 hool Parking Lot will not be permitted to leave for at least 1 hour after 
 the event ends. Please plan accordingly. Parking to support cheerleaders.\
 nIn order to accommodate the heavy traffic associated with the 3rd of July
  events at Keiser Park the following closures will be enforced beginning a
 bout 9:00 p.m.\n\nClosures at Windsor Road and the intersections of Winema
 ker Way and Cork Street.\nThe designated exits out of the Vintana Subdivis
 ion will be at Oak to Reiman and Burgundy to Starr.\nThere will be NO PARK
 ING on Windsor River Road between Starr and Windsor Road. This section of 
 Windsor River Road will be closed from about 8:00 a.m. to 11:00 p.m.\nAll 
 vehicles parked in the Windsor High School parking lot may be held for up 
 to 60 minutes after the fireworks as foot traffic clears.
